Prove that for the system of equations
\[
\begin{cases}
\frac{2}{x}+\frac{4}{x - 1}+\frac{6}{x - 2}+\frac{8}{x - 3}=-\frac{8}{15}\\
\frac{5}{x}+\frac{5}{x - 1}+\frac{5}{x - 2}+\frac{5}{x - 3}=\frac{16}{3}
\end{cases}
\]
if the shared rational solution is expressed as \(\frac{m}{n}\) in its simplest form, then \(m + n = 7\).

